--># Parallel Planner Contest

<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "Dispatch multiple planners in parallel, hold the contest open until every live plan is approved and no planner is mid-revision, then have the reviewer select the strongest qualifier.\n",
  codex: "Spawn multiple planner children in parallel plus one reviewer, hold the contest open until every live plan is approved and no planner is mid-revision, then have the reviewer select the strongest qualifier.\n",
  opencode: "Spawn multiple planner children in parallel plus one reviewer, hold the contest open until every live plan is approved and no planner is mid-revision, then have the reviewer select the strongest qualifier.\n",
  antigravity: "Dispatch multiple planners in parallel, hold the contest open until every live plan is approved and no planner is mid-revision, then have the reviewer select the strongest qualifier.\n"
}) %>
<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "",
  codex: "The orchestrator runs the contest as an ephemeral spawn tree: the planners and the reviewer are children spawned directly under the orchestrator. There is no team and no settlement handshake. All coordination is orchestrator-mediated — planners report up to the orchestrator, the orchestrator relays research and critiques between children, and the orchestrator routes the reviewer's findings and verdicts. The orchestrator decides closure by looking at the contest's state it has assembled from those reports, not by collecting confirmations from a peer roster.\n\n",
  opencode: "The orchestrator runs the contest as an ephemeral spawn tree: the planners and the reviewer are children spawned directly under the orchestrator. There is no team and no settlement handshake. All coordination is orchestrator-mediated — planners report up to the orchestrator, the orchestrator relays research and critiques between children, and the orchestrator routes the reviewer's findings and verdicts. The orchestrator decides closure by looking at the contest's state it has assembled from those reports, not by collecting confirmations from a peer roster.\n\n",
  antigravity: ""
}) %>Approval is the *qualifying bar*, not the finish line — `APPROVED` is sticky-but-revocable (see `<definitions>` and Closure below).

<definitions>

<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "**Live planner.** A planner that has not DM'd `PLAN: BLOCKED for:planner-N` and has not been ruled `VERDICT: BLOCKED for:planner-N` by the reviewer. The set of live planners shrinks over the contest as planners self-quit or are disqualified.\n\n**Supersession.** A later DM for the same subject supersedes earlier ones — this is how revocation works: a `VERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED for:planner-N round-K` arriving after a `VERDICT: APPROVED` for that same round revokes the approval.\n",
  codex: "**Live planner.** A planner that has not reported `PLAN: BLOCKED for:planner_N` and has not been ruled `VERDICT: BLOCKED for:planner_N` by the reviewer. The set of live planners shrinks over the contest as planners self-quit or are disqualified. The orchestrator tracks the live set from the reports it has collected.\n",
  opencode: "**Live planner.** A planner that has not reported `PLAN: BLOCKED for:planner_N` and has not been ruled `VERDICT: BLOCKED for:planner_N` by the reviewer. The set of live planners shrinks over the contest as planners self-quit or are disqualified. The orchestrator tracks the live set from the reports it has collected.\n",
  antigravity: "**Live planner.** A planner that has not DM'd `PLAN: BLOCKED for:planner-N` and has not been ruled `VERDICT: BLOCKED for:planner-N` by the reviewer. The set of live planners shrinks over the contest as planners self-quit or are disqualified.\n\n**Supersession.** A later DM for the same subject supersedes earlier ones — this is how revocation works: a `VERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED for:planner-N round-K` arriving after a `VERDICT: APPROVED` for that same round revokes the approval.\n"
}) %>
<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "**Idle notification.** The agent's process has stopped; it runs again only when an inbound message wakes it. Idle with nothing owed (approved and not revising; verdict delivered) is settled. Idle while owing a response, with nothing queued to wake it, is a stall — its last stated intent did not survive the idle. DM it what it needs to continue.\n",
  codex: "**Most recent report.** When multiple reports of the same shape exist for the same subject (e.g., several `VERDICT:` reports for `planner_1 round-1`), \"most recent\" means the latest one the orchestrator received. A later report for the same subject supersedes earlier ones — this is how revocation works: a `VERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED for:planner_N round-K` that arrives after a `VERDICT: APPROVED for:planner_N round-K` revokes the earlier approval.\n",
  opencode: "**Most recent report.** When multiple reports of the same shape exist for the same subject (e.g., several `VERDICT:` reports for `planner_1 round-1`), \"most recent\" means the latest one the orchestrator received. A later report for the same subject supersedes earlier ones — this is how revocation works: a `VERDICT: CHANGES_REQUESTED for:planner_N round-K` that arrives after a `VERDICT: APPROVED for:planner_N round-K` revokes the earlier approval.\n",
  antigravity: "**Idle notification.** The agent's process has stopped; it runs again only when an inbound message wakes it. Idle with nothing owed (approved and not revising; verdict delivered) is settled. Idle while owing a response, with nothing queued to wake it, is a stall — its last stated intent did not survive the idle. DM it what it needs to continue.\n"
}) %>
</definitions>

<placeholder-variables>
[N_PLANNERS] — Number of parallel planners, chosen by the caller (2–4) by the size of the solution space
<%= it.variant({
  "claude-code": "[PLANNER_MODEL] — Chosen per planner slot: the model that handles most planning work reliably by default; mix in the strongest available model for slots facing the deepest unknowns\n[REVIEWER_MODEL] — Chosen by the same unknowns-depth judgment as `[PLANNER_MODEL]`: the strongest available model when the contest's unknowns run deep, otherwise the model that handles most review work reliably\n[WINNING_PLANNER] — The `planner-N` subagent the reviewer named in its `WINNER:` DM\n[WINNING_SLUG] — Semantically descriptive slug chosen from the winner's most recent `PLAN: READY` DM (e.g., `initial`, `phase-2`, `schema-first`)\n",
  codex: "[PLANNER_EFFORT] — Chosen per planner slot: the effort tier that handles most planning work reliably by default; mix in the deepest tier for slots facing the deepest unknowns\n[REVIEWER_EFFORT] — Chosen by the same unknowns-depth judgment as `[PLANNER_EFFORT]`: the deepest tier when the contest's unknowns run deep, otherwise the tier that handles most review work reliably\n[WINNING_PLANNER] — The `planner_N` child the reviewer named in its `WINNER:` report\n[WINNING_SLUG] — Semantically descriptive slug chosen from the winner's most recent `PLAN: READY` report (e.g., `initial`, `phase-2`, `schema-first`)\n",
  opencode: "[PLANNER_EFFORT] — Chosen per planner slot: the effort tier that handles most planning work reliably by default; mix in the deepest tier for slots facing the deepest unknowns\n[REVIEWER_EFFORT] — Chosen by the same unknowns-depth judgment as `[PLANNER_EFFORT]`: the deepest tier when the contest's unknowns run deep, otherwise the tier that handles most review work reliably\n[WINNING_PLANNER] — The `planner_N` child the reviewer named in its `WINNER:` report\n[WINNING_SLUG] — Semantically descriptive slug chosen from the winner's most recent `PLAN: READY` report (e.g., `initial`, `phase-2`, `schema-first`)\n",
  antigravity: "[PLANNER_MODEL] — Chosen per planner slot: the model that handles most planning work reliably by default; mix in the strongest available model for slots facing the deepest unknowns\n[REVIEWER_MODEL] — Chosen by the same unknowns-depth judgment as `[PLANNER_MODEL]`: the strongest available model when the contest's unknowns run deep, otherwise the model that handles most review work reliably\n[WINNING_PLANNER] — The `planner-N` subagent the reviewer named in its `WINNER:` DM\n[WINNING_SLUG] — Semantically descriptive slug chosen from the winner's most recent `PLAN: READY` DM (e.g., `initial`, `phase-2`, `schema-first`)\n"
}) %>[PRE_EXISTING_UNAPPROVED_FILES] — Un-approved plan files (and sidecars) that existed before the contest and were not seeded as the incumbent; empty when none
</placeholder-variables>

